[Retroactive note added later, per the Symptom/Ruled out/Root cause/Fix commit-message framework]

Symptom: README described the original VMware/Gepard Shield problem as
generic "VM detection."

Ruled out: the theory that Gepard Shield was detecting/blocking generic
virtualization as such.

Root cause: the actual incompatibility was Gepard Shield's compatibility
with Windows 11 on ARM specifically — the guest OS a VM on Apple Silicon
is forced to run — not VM-detection evasion in general.

Fix: corrected the README's problem description accordingly (this commit
began a short series of follow-up wording passes to align the rest of
the README with the corrected root cause).
